The code statements that lead to the bug are:
RAS_DEV_ERR(ras_core->dev, "Failed to detect ras interrupt!\n");
Reason:
When ras_core is NULL, the preceding condition fails and execution reaches this line, which dereferences ras_core->dev, causing a NULL pointer dereference.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (ras_core && ras_core->dev)
    RAS_DEV_ERR(ras_core->dev, "Failed to detect ras interrupt!\n");
Reason:
This adds a NULL check for both ras_core and ras_core->dev before accessing ras_core->dev, preventing the NULL pointer dereference.

